is a `NoisyAttitudeSensor` running on its own 100 Hz clock, so the autopilot
reads a biased, noisy, quantised and already-held signal rather than the
truth. Comparing the two harnesses isolates the sensor from everything else.

The bias is the interesting term. A standing 0.5 deg of pitch bias is an
error the loop *cannot* reject: the integrator drives the measured attitude
onto the command, which puts the true attitude 0.5 deg away from it, so the
aircraft settles into a slightly different climb and stays there. Noise and
quantisation, by contrast, mostly average out of the attitude and show up in
